01:36:30.463 --> 01:36:35.125
It's so interesting that
it's what it became about.

01:36:35.125 --> 01:36:36.416
But you're totally right.

01:36:36.416 --> 01:36:40.750
Most reasonable Christians
of all stripes will be like,

01:36:40.750 --> 01:36:42.209
"Yeah, yeah, completely agree with this,"

01:36:42.209 --> 01:36:44.117
like, "That's not what the gospel's about,

01:36:44.117 --> 01:36:47.367
it's not about all these other things."

01:36:48.815 --> 01:36:49.648
So, yeah.

01:36:53.919 --> 01:36:55.700
Yeah, I think ultimately
this is all pretty,

01:36:55.700 --> 01:36:57.117
like, soft stuff.

01:37:00.295 --> 01:37:02.909
The point of this album
was not to condemn.

01:37:02.909 --> 01:37:03.742
It's just-

01:37:03.742 --> 01:37:04.857
The Supreme Court case,

01:37:04.857 --> 01:37:08.671
I mean, that's something that I think it,

01:37:08.671 --> 01:37:10.419
there's a couple of
places where it starts to-

01:37:10.419 --> 01:37:15.419
Well, and this song was
written before the Roe v. Wade

01:37:15.434 --> 01:37:17.101
that was overturned.

01:37:18.148 --> 01:37:22.559
It wasn't in anticipation of
that particular case even.

01:37:22.559 --> 01:37:24.602
There's always a Supreme Court case

01:37:24.602 --> 01:37:27.645
that Christians think that
God is on the side of an issue

01:37:27.645 --> 01:37:29.387
and that that's what Jesus would believe

01:37:29.387 --> 01:37:31.002
and that's probably the best one,

01:37:31.002 --> 01:37:32.747
is that they just fundamentally believe

01:37:32.747 --> 01:37:36.363
Jesus would be pro-life
no questions asked.

01:37:36.363 --> 01:37:39.198
And it's just like, "Really, though?"

01:37:39.198 --> 01:37:41.435
Like, "You really think that?

01:37:41.435 --> 01:37:45.225
Show me the biblical evidence of that."

01:37:45.225 --> 01:37:49.642
So anyway, I think this is,
again, it's not like I'm,

01:37:51.037 --> 01:37:52.531
like, if you're a Christian

01:37:52.531 --> 01:37:53.610
and you're conservative Christian

01:37:53.610 --> 01:37:55.607
and you completely,
fundamentally disagree with me

01:37:55.607 --> 01:37:57.303
and you've made it to
this point in the album,

01:37:57.303 --> 01:38:00.592
it's like, okay, these songs
may be challenging for you.

01:38:00.592 --> 01:38:02.084
But, again, this wasn't about,

01:38:02.084 --> 01:38:05.626
"Hey, this is a message for
the church first and foremost."

01:38:05.626 --> 01:38:10.043
It is, but it's more like
when you are deconstructing

01:38:11.658 --> 01:38:13.988
or deconverting, like,
there's a lot of things

01:38:13.988 --> 01:38:16.319
that you're thinking and
you're beginning to see things.

01:38:16.319 --> 01:38:17.612
You're like, "Man, like, this was the way

01:38:17.612 --> 01:38:18.823
that it always was.

01:38:18.823 --> 01:38:19.863
This is how we thought.

01:38:19.863 --> 01:38:21.520
We were so offended by this thing,

01:38:21.520 --> 01:38:23.232
but, you know, all this other
stuff didn't offend us,"

01:38:23.232 --> 01:38:26.211
and that's weird and hypocritical.

01:38:26.211 --> 01:38:28.530
And you just see it and
you wanna talk about it,

01:38:28.530 --> 01:38:33.098
you wanna say it, you wanna
point out the hypocrisy.

01:38:33.098 --> 01:38:38.098
But this next song, "Fruit",
is even more specifically

01:38:38.384 --> 01:38:42.301
